    "body": "> If it's the document associated with `url` it can't be null, since we don't know that synchronously.\r\n\r\nRight, but I think the question is: is there any mechanism that should set `popup.window` to null asynchronously (as Chromium does at least) _after_ the browsing context group switch is performed, to ensure that the opener doesn't continue to hold a handle to the _new_ Window loaded in the popup, which now lives in another BCG.",
